  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Comprehensive and integrated social protection systems strengthened and progressively introduced in line with International Social Security Standards.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The prolonged socio-economic crisis in the Occupied Palestinian Territory has increased pressure on existing social protection systems and highlighted the need for more integrated, inclusive, and coordinated policy responses that support workers and employers throughout life and work transitions. In this context, the ILO supports national efforts to strengthen governance, coordination, and evidence-based monitoring of social protection policies and strategies in line with international social security standards and principles of social dialogue.

The intervention focuses on developing and operationalizing a national monitoring framework for social protection policies and strategies that enables government institutions and workers&#x2019; and employers&#x2019; organizations to jointly monitor implementation progress, identify policy gaps, and support evidence-based decision-making. Through strengthened institutional coordination and participatory monitoring mechanisms, the intervention aims to improve the responsiveness, coherence, and effectiveness of social protection policies and programmes, particularly for vulnerable populations and workers affected by economic and labour market transitions.</narrative>
  </description>
